\begin{align}
\text{Probability of guessing correctly} &= \frac{\text{{number of correct papers}}}{\text{{total number of papers}}}\\
&= \frac{16}{20}
\end{align}

Simplifying, we get:

\begin{align}
&= \frac{4 \cdot 4}{5 \cdot 4} & (\text{{factoring 16 as }}4 \cdot 4)\\
&= \frac{4}{5}
\end{align}

So the probability of guessing correctly is $\boxed{\frac{4}{5}}$.

