The volume of a $2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm}$ cube is:
\begin{align}
6 \text{ cm}^3  &&  \text{(because } \boxed{ 2 \times 2 \times 2 = 8 } \text{ cm}^3 \text{ and subtracting the original volume)}\\
19 \text{ cm}^3 &&\text{(adding 19 to the original volume)}
\end{align}

\begin{align}
\text{Find next cube edge length, }\ 6 \text{ cm}^3 + 19 \text{ cm}^3 = \boxed{ 25 } \text{ cm}^3
\end{align}
Now, we have the volume of the new cube. Since the cube has only three side lengths,
each side must be equal. Thus, if $x$ is the edge size of the new cube, we have:
$$(x * x * x) = 25 \text{ cm}^3 \Rightarrow x^3 = 25 \Rightarrow x = \sqrt[3]{25}. $$ Since one of our numbers has three digits,
the cube root has three digits also. Thus,
\begin{align}
x = \boxed{ \sqrt[3]{25} \text{ cm} } = \boxed{ 5 \text{ cm} } && \text{(since } \sqrt[3]{25} = 5 \text{ to the nearest integer)}
